  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Principle of Strong Induction}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "Theorem:\ngiven: P(n_) is (_ is \\natural) -> (_ is \\\\statement)\nwhere:\n. forAll: n is \\natural\n  then:\n  . if:\n    . forAll: k is \\natural\n      where:\n      . k \\:natural.leq?:/ n\n      . k != n\n      then: P(k)\n    then: P(n)\nthen:\n. forAll: n is \\natural\n  then: P(n)\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Principle of Strong Induction\"\n. description: \"If $P(n)$ follows from the validity of $P(k)$ at every preceding\n                natural number $k<n$, then $P$ holds for every natural number.\"\nId: \"844c54eb-187b-4369-8fd2-84d5d7da2b4b\"",
